{"title":"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #17</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #19</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A jar contains quarters (worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcfc22da43fe3886c3ff0069a4ade504c70d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> each), nickels (worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83eb1662269aa1002f1aaeccaeaeaec23827f90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> each), and pennies (worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b66729b2443c4ecd87e2267df87d38f4a8bc57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.01$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> each).  The value of the quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be68b67793eb8fb9df7111777d94b145767394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. The value of the nickels is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be68b67793eb8fb9df7111777d94b145767394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. The value of the pennies is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be68b67793eb8fb9df7111777d94b145767394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. If Judith randomly chooses one coin from the jar, what is the probability that it is a quarter?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055e2388cf388b24ff0006594bde5a58ceed1da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{25}{31} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{31} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{5}{248} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"453\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the total value of the coins divided by how much each coin is worth, we can find out how many quarters, nickels, and pennies there are. This would allow us to find the probability of picking a quarter by dividing the number of quarters by the total number of coins.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/08600e828ff66abf5f516b1d215274ac04872a55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10.00}{0.25} = \\frac{10.00 \\times 4}{0.25 \\times 4} = \\frac{40.00}{1} = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"260\" height=\"40\" /> quarters.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41d961027b47f0c5ab365c2f2b80072aee720ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10.00}{0.05} = \\frac{10.00 \\times 20}{0.05 \\times 20} = \\frac{200.00}{1} = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"288\" height=\"40\" /> nickels.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/25697b6e5cfb8dcc5c339ccc3665237955e4dae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10.00}{0.01} = \\frac{10.00 \\times 100}{0.01 \\times 100} = \\frac{1000.00}{1} = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"315\" height=\"40\" /> pennies.\n</p><p>This means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56be1bc26a4fed8dfdf6fa1fee09578a873fef1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 + 200 + 1000 = 1240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" /> coins altogether.\n</p><p>Dividing the number of quarters by the total number of coins, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6af02b6fbb1b759c9540044c3234b5359da3866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{1240} = \\frac{1}{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a hr